    <innerclass refid="classDatabaseBusy" prot="public">DatabaseBusy</innerclass>
    <briefdescription>
<para>Exception signalling that the connection pool could not lease a connection in time. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This header defines <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref>, a tiny exception class used as a signal. It adds no data of its own; it simply derives from std::runtime_error with a default message so it can be caught either specifically or by generic error handlers. Its whole purpose is to give &quot;the pool is exhausted&quot; a distinct type.</para>
<para>WHY THIS FILE MATTERS IN THE SERVER: The HTTP layer needs to tell two very different failures apart: a broken query (probably a server bug, answer 500) and a temporary shortage of connections (the client should retry, answer 503 with Retry-After). <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool_1a39716826b3e5be2f15603d8cf809446b" kindref="member">DatabaseConnectionPool::get_connection()</ref> throws this type when its wait expires, and filters, controllers and the watchdog all catch it separately. Without a dedicated type, every timeout would look like a generic error and clients would not know to retry.</para>
<para>CONCEPTS TO LEARN (for beginners):<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Exceptions and catch blocks: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/try_catch</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>std::runtime_error (a standard exception carrying a message): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/runtime_error">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/error/runtime_error</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Inheritance: <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/derived_class">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/derived_class</ulink></para>
</listitem><listitem><para>HTTP 503 <ref refid="classService" kindref="compound">Service</ref> Unavailable and Retry-After</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>explicit constructors (prevent accidental implicit conversion): <ulink url="https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/explicit">https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/language/explicit</ulink></para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Amr Osman <ulink url="mailto:dr3mro@gmail.com">dr3mro@gmail.com</ulink> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="date"><para>2026-11-16 </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
